    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12640" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dēductōrĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>for drawing off</i> or <i>draining</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">medicamenta,</span>”
				<i>aperient, purgative</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
					Aur. Acut. 2, 19</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cuniculus (in stabulis),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Veg. Vet. 1, 56</span></i>
			. Also <i>subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">deducto-rium</span></b> , ii, n.,
				<i>a drain</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">liquoris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pall. Nov. 7, 21</span></i>
			.</div>
